    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0468" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72112Aml/38</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Belt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-06T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 2, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d431-f1"/> and February 4, 11
                        a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d431-f2"/> Text of note of Honduran Government
                    dated January 27, amended and corrected by your telegram February 3,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d431-f3"/> was transmitted to War Trade Board for its
                    consideration. The guarantees of the Honduran Government appear satisfactory and
                    resumption of traffic to Amapala through agent of Pacific Mail is approved.</p>
                <p>This information has been communicated to Rosseter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
